{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T16:29:40.211520", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the item in the environment\n  item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]  # This is the index of the item in the environment\n\n  # Check if we have all the required primitives for the item\n  required_primitives = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item_index)\n  # Check if we have all the required primitives for the item\n  if not all(env._current_state.inventory[prim_idx] > 0 for prim_idx in required_primitives):\n    return []  # Return empty list if primitives are missing\n\n  # Get the workshop index from the recipe\n  workshop = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index][\"_at\"]\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop]  # Get the index of the workshop\n\n  # Get the position of the workshop\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(env._current_state.grid.shape[0]):\n    for j in range(env._current_state.grid.shape[1]):\n      if env._current_state.grid[i, j, workshop_index] > 0:\n        workshop_pos = (i, j)\n        break\n    if workshop_pos:\n      break\n\n  # If workshop is not found, return empty list\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Calculate the direction to move to reach the workshop\n  dir = env._current_state.pos[0] - workshop_pos[0], env._current_state.pos[1] - workshop_pos[1]\n  # Convert direction to a direction index\n  if dir == (0, -1):\n    dir_idx = 0  # LEFT\n  elif dir == (0, 1):\n    dir_idx = 1  # RIGHT\n  elif dir == (-1, 0):\n    dir_idx = 2  # UP\n  elif dir == (1, 0):\n    dir_idx = 3  # DOWN\n  else:\n    return []  # Invalid direction\n\n  # Return the move action to reach the workshop\n  return [dir_idx] + [USE]  # Use the workshop to craft the item", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
