{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T16:32:35.336214", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Step 1: Check if the item can be crafted by checking its recipe in the environment's cookbook.\n  # Step 2: If the recipe exists, determine the required workshop for crafting.\n  # Step 3: Check if all required primitives are available in the inventory.\n  # Step 4: If all primitives are available, move to the workshop location and perform the USE action.\n  # Step 5: If any primitive is missing, return an empty list.\n\n  # For example, to craft an axe (which requires 1 stick and 1 iron), the sequence of actions would be:\n  # 1. Collect stick if not already in inventory.\n  # 2. Collect iron if not already in inventory.\n  # 3. Move to the workshop location (e.g., workshop0).\n  # 4. Perform USE action to craft the axe.\n\n  # Note: The environment's cookbook is accessible via `env.world.cookbook`.\n  # The `env.world.cookbook.index` provides a mapping from item names to indices.\n  # The `env.world.cookbook.recipes` contains the recipes in the format:\n  # {output_index: {ingredient_index: count, ...}}\n  # The `env.world.cookbook.recipes[output_index].get('_at')` gives the workshop location.\n\n  # To check if an item is in the inventory, use:\n  # `env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[item]] > 0`\n\n  # To get the workshop location, use:\n  # `workshop = env.world.cookbook.recipes[output_index].get('_at')`\n  # Note: workshop will be one of \"workshop0\", \"workshop1\", or \"workshop2\".\n\n  # To move to the workshop location, you need to find the position of the workshop on the grid.\n  # The grid is accessible via `env._current_state.grid`, which is of shape (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  # You can find the position of the workshop by:\n  # `workshop_pos = np.where(env._current_state.grid[..., env.world.cookbook.index[workshop]] > 0)`\n  # Note: workshop_pos will be a tuple of arrays (rows, cols), so you need to get the first occurrence.\n\n  # Once you have the workshop position, you need to move the agent to that position.\n  # The agent can move using the MOVE_FUNC with direction (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT).\n  # You need to compute the direction to move based on the current position and workshop position.\n\n  # Finally, perform the USE action (action index 4) to craft the item.\n\n  # If any step fails (e.g., missing primitive, workshop not found), return an empty list.\n\n  # Note: The function should return an empty list if any of the conditions are not met (e.g., missing primitive, workshop not found).\n\n  # Note: The environment's state is accessible via `env._current_state`.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
