{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T16:36:46.783427", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is a primitive. If so, we don't need to craft it.\n  if item in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n    return []\n\n  # Get the recipe for the item.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item)\n\n  # If the item is not craftable, return an empty list.\n  if recipe is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Check if we have all the required items.\n  # Get the current inventory of the environment.\n  inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  # Get the required items from the recipe.\n  required_items = recipe.copy()\n  # Remove the \"_at\" key from the recipe.\n  required_items.pop(\"_at\", None)\n\n  # Check if we have all the required items.\n  for req_item, count in required_items.items():\n    if inventory[req_item] < count:\n      return []  # Not enough items to craft.\n\n  # Find the workshop where we can craft the item.\n  workshop = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  # Get the index of the workshop.\n  workshop_index = env.world.index.get(workshop)\n\n  # Go to the workshop.\n  # The workshop is a specific location in the grid, so we need to move to it.\n  # We'll generate a path to the workshop using a pathfinding algorithm.\n  # However, since this is a simple grid, we can use a simple greedy approach.\n  # Find the nearest workshop cell in the grid.\n  # We'll search for the nearest cell with the workshop_index.\n  # The grid is of shape (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(grid.shape[0]):\n    for j in range(grid.shape[1]):\n      if grid[i, j, workshop_index] == 1:\n        workshop_pos = (i, j)\n        break\n    if workshop_pos:\n      break\n\n  # If no workshop is found, return an empty list.\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Move to the workshop.\n  # We'll generate a sequence of moves to get to the workshop.\n  # We'll use a simple pathfinding algorithm to get from the current position to the workshop.\n  # However, in this implementation, we'll just move in a straight line towards the workshop.\n  # This is a simplified version; a full pathfinding algorithm would be more robust.\n  current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  path = []\n  if current_pos[0] < workshop_pos[0]:\n    path.extend([DOWN] * (workshop_pos[0] - current_pos[0]))\n  elif current_pos[0] > workshop_pos[0]:\n    path.extend([UP] * (current_pos[0] - workshop_pos[0]))\n  if current_pos[1] < workshop_pos[1]:\n    path.extend([RIGHT] * (workshop_pos[1] - current_pos[1]))\n  elif current_pos[1] > workshop_pos[1]:\n    path.extend([LEFT] * (current_pos[1] - workshop_pos[1]))\n\n  # Now, we need to perform the USE action at the workshop.\n  path.append(USE)\n\n  return path", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
