{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T19:52:29.929901", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is craftable\n  # If not, return empty list\n  # If yes, then:\n  # 1. Check if we have all the primitives required for crafting.\n  # 2. If not, return empty list (we need to collect those primitives first).\n  # 3. If we have the required primitives, then:\n  #    a. Go to the workshop where the item can be crafted (specified in the recipe).\n  #    b. Perform the USE action to craft the item.\n  #    c. Return the sequence of actions.\n  #\n  # Note: The `env` is a CraftLab instance. The `item` is a string (e.g., \"AXE\"), and we need to find its corresponding index in the env.world.cookbook.index.\n  #\n  # Hint: You can use env.world.cookbook.recipes to access the recipes.\n  # Hint: You can use env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item) to get the required primitives for the item.\n  # Hint: You can use env.world.cookbook.index to get the index of the item.\n  # Hint: You can use env.world.cookbook.environment to get the environment indices.\n  # Hint: You can use env.world.workshop_indices to get the list of workshop indices.\n\n  return []", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
