{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T20:45:06.043690", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is craftable.\n  # If not, return an empty list of actions.\n  # If it is craftable, go to the workshop (specified in the recipe) to craft it.\n\n  # We assume the item is a string. We need to convert it to an index.\n  # We can use env.world.cookbook.index[item] to get the index.\n  # We need to get the recipe for the item.\n\n  # We need to check if we have all the required primitives for the recipe.\n  # We can use env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index] to get the recipe.\n  # The recipe is a dictionary with keys being the primitive names and values being the counts.\n  # We need to check if the agent's inventory has at least the required counts for each primitive.\n\n  # If we don't have the required primitives, we need to collect them.\n  # We can use the collect function to collect the required primitives.\n  # But note: the collect function takes a primitive string, not an index.\n\n  # We need to get the list of required primitives from the recipe.\n\n  # Then, for each required primitive, if we don't have enough, we need to collect it.\n\n  # After collecting all required primitives, we need to go to the workshop specified in the recipe.\n  # The workshop is specified by the \"_at\" key in the recipe.\n  # The workshop index can be obtained from env.world.cookbook.index[workshop_name].\n  # But note: the workshop name might be \"workshop0\", \"workshop1\", or \"workshop2\".\n  # We need to move to the workshop location.\n\n  # We need to move to the workshop. We can use the move function to move to the workshop.\n  # But note: the move function takes a direction, not a position. We need to move in the direction of the workshop.\n\n  # How to find the direction of the workshop?\n  # We need to find the position of the workshop in the grid.\n  # The grid is stored in env.world.cookbook.index.\n  # We can get the grid from env._current_state.grid.\n  # The grid is a 3D array of shape (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds).\n  # We need to find the position where the workshop kind is present.\n\n  # But note: the workshop kind might be present in multiple positions. We need to find the nearest one.\n  # We can use the agent's current position to find the nearest workshop.\n\n  # Once we are at the workshop, we need to perform the USE action to craft the item.\n\n  # We need to return the list of actions to craft the item.\n\n  # Return the list of actions.\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
