{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T21:36:23.448462", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # We're going to implement this function\n  # The following are the steps:\n  # 1. Check if the agent has all the required primitives to craft the item.\n  # 2. If not, then we need to collect the missing primitives.\n  # 3. Once we have all the required primitives, we need to go to the workshop specified in the recipe.\n  # 4. Then, we need to perform the USE action at the workshop to craft the item.\n  # 5. We need to return the sequence of actions to achieve the above.\n  # 6. The actions should be in the order of: move to the workshop (if needed), then perform the USE action.\n  # 7. We need to handle the case where the agent is already at the workshop.\n\n  # We will use the following functions:\n  # - env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal): returns a dict of primitives required to craft the item.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index.get(item): returns the index of the item.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index]: returns the recipe for the item.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index][\"_at\"]: returns the workshop index where the item can be crafted.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index.get(workshop): returns the index of the workshop.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive): returns the index of the primitive.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index][primitive_index]: returns the quantity of the primitive required.\n\n  # We will use the following helper functions:\n  # - get_workshop_index(workshop_name): returns the index of the workshop.\n  # - get_primitive_index(primitive_name): returns the index of the primitive.\n\n  # We will use the following action functions:\n  # - move_to_workshop(workshop_index): returns a list of move actions to go to the workshop.\n  # - craft_at_workshop(): returns the USE action at the workshop.\n\n  # We will use the following environment methods:\n  # - env.world.cookbook: the cookbook instance.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index: the index instance.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.recipes: the recipes dictionary.\n  # - env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item): returns the primitives required for the item.\n\n  # We will use the following state methods:\n  # - env._current_state: the current state of the environment.\n  # - env._current_state.pos: the current position of the agent.\n  # - env._current_state.dir: the current direction of the agent.\n  # - env._current_state.inventory: the current inventory of the agent.\n\n  # We will use the following action constants:\n  # - UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE: the action indices.\n\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
