{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T22:11:29.339150", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # If the item is already crafted, return empty action list.\n  if env._current_state.satisfies(\"goal\", env.world.cookbook.index[item]):\n    return []\n  \n  # Get the recipe for the item from the cookbook.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[env.world.cookbook.index[item]]\n  \n  # Check if all required primitives are present in the inventory.\n  for primitive, count in recipe.items():\n    if primitive == \"_at\":\n      continue\n    if count > env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]]:\n      # If not, we need to collect the missing primitive.\n      return collect(env, primitive)\n  \n  # If all primitives are available, we need to go to the workshop.\n  workshop = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  # Find the workshop index in the environment.\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop]\n  \n  # Get the current position and direction.\n  pos = env._current_state.pos\n  dir = env._current_state.dir\n  \n  # Check if we are already at the workshop.\n  if workshop_index in env._current_state.grid[pos[0], pos[1]]:\n    # If at the workshop, perform the USE action.\n    return [env.action_specs()[\"USE\"]]\n  \n  # Otherwise, move to the workshop.\n  # We need to find the nearest workshop to move to.\n  # Since the environment is a grid, we can use BFS to find the nearest workshop.\n  # But for simplicity, we assume the workshop is at a fixed position for now.\n  # This is a placeholder and needs to be implemented.\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
