{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T22:24:41.280516", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is craftable\n  if item not in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n      return []  # Item not craftable\n\n  # Get the recipe for the item\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item]\n\n  # Check if we have all the required ingredients\n  for ingredient, count in recipe.items():\n      if ingredient == \"_at\":\n          continue  # Skip the workshop location\n      if env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[ingredient]] < count:\n          return []  # Not enough ingredients, return empty list\n\n  # Find the workshop where the item can be crafted\n  workshop = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop]\n\n  # Check if we are at the workshop\n  if env._current_state.next_to(workshop_index):\n      # We are at the workshop, so craft the item\n      return [env.action_specs()[\"USE\"]]  # Assuming USE is the action to craft\n\n  # If we're not at the workshop, move to it\n  # Find the direction to the nearest workshop (this is a simplified example)\n  # We'll assume we move towards the workshop in the grid\n  # This part needs to be implemented properly\n  # For now, we'll return an empty list as a placeholder\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
