{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T22:42:03.198745", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # We are going to use the following helper functions:\n  # - get_goal_index: returns the index of the item in the environment\n  # - get_primitives_for: returns the required primitives for the item\n  # - get_workshop: returns the workshop where the item can be crafted\n  # - get_recipe: returns the recipe for the item\n  # - get_current_inventory: returns the current inventory of the agent\n  # - get_current_position: returns the current position of the agent\n  # - is_at_workshop: checks if the agent is at the workshop where the item can be crafted\n  # - move_to_workshop: moves the agent to the workshop where the item can be crafted\n  # - craft_at_workshop: crafts the item at the workshop\n  # - is_item_collected: checks if the item is collected in the inventory\n  # - collect_item: collects the item from the grid\n  \n  # However, note that we are only allowed to implement the functions that are in the DSL code base. \n  # We cannot implement new helper functions, but we can use the existing functions in the environment.\n  # We will use the following functions from the environment:\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index: gives the index for the item\n  # - env.world.cookbook.primitives_for: gives the required primitives for the item\n  # - env.world.cookbook.recipes: gives the recipe for the item\n  # - env._current_state.inventory: gives the current inventory\n  # - env._current_state.pos: gives the current position\n  # - env.world.workshop_indices: gives the list of workshop indices\n  # - env.world.water_index: gives the water index\n  # - env.world.stone_index: gives the stone index\n  # - env.step(action): steps the environment with the given action\n\n  return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
