{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T22:48:10.480379", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # If the item is not in the cookbook, return empty list\n  if item not in env.world.cookbook.index:\n    return []\n\n  # Get the index of the item in the cookbook\n  item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  \n  # Get the recipe for the item\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item_idx)\n  if recipe is None:\n    return []  # No recipe found for the item\n\n  # Check if the agent has all the required items\n  inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  for ingredient, count in recipe.items():\n    if ingredient == \"_at\":\n      workshop = count  # This is the workshop index\n      continue\n    ingredient_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.get(ingredient)\n    if ingredient_idx is None or inventory[ingredient_idx] < count:\n      return []  # Not enough ingredients\n\n  # If we have all the ingredients, craft the item\n  # Find the workshop where the item can be crafted\n  workshop = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.get(workshop)\n  if workshop_idx is None:\n    return []  # Workshop not found\n\n  # Go to the workshop\n  # We need to find a path to the workshop location\n  # For now, we'll assume the workshop is at a specific location\n  # We can use a simple pathfinding to move to the workshop\n  # This is a placeholder for the actual pathfinding logic\n\n  # For now, assume the workshop is at (1, 1) for simplicity\n  # In reality, we'd need to find the nearest workshop location\n  target_pos = (1, 1)  # Placeholder\n\n  # Generate move actions to reach the workshop\n  # This is a simplified version; actual pathfinding would be needed\n  actions = []\n  # Move to the target position\n  # This would require a pathfinding algorithm to generate the correct moves\n  # For now, we'll assume we can move directly\n  # We need to compute the direction to move\n  current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  dx = target_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n  dy = target_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n  if dx > 0:\n    actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n  elif dx < 0:\n    actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n  if dy > 0:\n    actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n  elif dy < 0:\n    actions.append(1)  # UP\n\n  # Perform the USE action at the workshop\n  actions.append(4)  # USE\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
