{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T23:50:03.308374", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if item is in the cookbook index\n  if item not in env.world.cookbook.index:\n      return []\n\n  item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n\n  # Check if the item is a primitive (can't craft primitives)\n  if item_index in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      return []\n\n  # Check if the item has a recipe\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item_index)\n  if recipe is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Check if all ingredients are available\n  for ingredient_index, amount in recipe.items():\n      if ingredient_index == \"_at\":\n          continue\n      # Check if we have enough of the ingredient\n      if ingredient_index >= len(env._current_state.inventory) or env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_index] < amount:\n          return []\n\n  # Get the workshop location from the recipe\n  workshop_location = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_location is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Extract workshop number from workshop_location (e.g., \"workshop0\" -> 0)\n  try:\n      workshop_num = int(workshop_location[-1])\n  except:\n      return []\n\n  # Get the workshop index from the environment's workshop_indices\n  if workshop_num < 0 or workshop_num >= len(env.world.workshop_indices):\n      return []\n\n  workshop_index = env.world.workshop_indices[workshop_num]\n\n  # Check if we are next to the workshop\n  if env._current_state.next_to(workshop_index):\n      # We are next to the workshop, so we can craft immediately\n      return [4]  # USE action\n\n  # If not, we need to move to the workshop location.\n  # But the environment doesn't provide a way to know the direction, so we'll assume a fixed sequence of moves.\n\n  # We'll try to move towards the workshop by checking the neighborhood.\n  # However, the environment doesn't provide a way to know the direction, so we can't generate a specific move.\n\n  # Since we can't determine the direction, we'll return an empty list meaning the agent cannot craft the item.\n  # In a real scenario, we would need a planner to find a path, but for now, we'll return an empty list.\n  return []  # Not next to the workshop, so cannot craft", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T23:50:05.287125", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if item is in the cookbook and not a primitive\n  if item not in env.world.cookbook.index:\n      return []\n  item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  if item_index in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      return []\n\n  # Get the recipe\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item_index)\n  if recipe is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Check ingredients\n  for ingredient_index, amount in recipe.items():\n      if ingredient_index == \"_at\":\n          continue\n      if ingredient_index >= len(env._current_state.inventory) or env._current_state.inventory[ingredient_index] < amount:\n          return []\n\n  # Get workshop location\n  workshop_location = recipe.get(\"_at\")\n  if workshop_location is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Extract workshop number from workshop_location (e.g., \"workshop0\" -> 0)\n  try:\n      workshop_num = int(workshop_location[-1])\n  except:\n      return []\n\n  # Get the workshop index from the environment's workshop_indices\n  if workshop_num < 0 or workshop_num >= len(env.world.workshop_indices):\n      return []\n\n  workshop_index = env.world.workshop_indices[workshop_num]\n\n  # Check if we are next to the workshop\n  if env._current_state.next_to(workshop_index):\n      return [4]  # USE action\n\n  # If not next to, we need to move towards the workshop.\n  # We'll try to move towards the workshop by checking the grid for the workshop location.\n  # However, we don't have a direct way to know the direction.\n\n  # Instead, we'll use a simple strategy: move in a fixed direction (e.g., UP) repeatedly until we are next to the workshop.\n  # But note: the environment doesn't provide a way to know the direction of the workshop.\n\n  # Given the problem constraints, we'll assume that the workshop is in a known location relative to the agent.\n  # For simplicity, we'll return a sequence of moves that might get us closer.\n\n  # However, we cannot know the exact direction, so we'll return an empty list.\n\n  return []  # Not next to the workshop, so cannot craft", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
