{"timestamp": "2025-09-13T00:11:26.773094", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # First, get the index of the item in the environment's cookbook.\n  item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  # Check if the item is in the recipes.\n  if item_index not in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n      # If the item is not a craftable item, return an empty list.\n      return []\n  \n  # Get the recipe for the item.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index]\n  # Get the workshop index where the item can be crafted.\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.index[recipe[\"_at\"]]\n  \n  # Check if the agent has all the required items to craft the item.\n  # We need to check if the agent has the required items in the inventory.\n  # The inventory is stored in env._current_state.inventory.\n  inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  # Check if the agent has all the required items.\n  for ingredient, count in recipe.items():\n      if ingredient == \"_at\":\n          continue\n      ingredient_index = env.world.cookbook.index[ingredient]\n      if inventory[ingredient_index] < count:\n          return []\n  \n  # If we have all the required items, we need to go to the workshop and craft the item.\n  # First, find the position of the workshop in the grid.\n  # The grid is stored in env._current_state.grid.\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(grid.shape[1]):\n          if grid[i, j, workshop_index] > 0:\n              workshop_pos = (i, j)\n              break\n      if workshop_pos:\n          break\n  \n  # If the workshop is not found, return an empty list.\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n      return []\n  \n  # Now, move the agent to the workshop position.\n  # We need to compute the direction to move to reach the workshop.\n  # The agent's current position is stored in env._current_state.pos.\n  pos = env._current_state.pos\n  # Compute the vector from current position to workshop position.\n  dx = workshop_pos[0] - pos[0]\n  dy = workshop_pos[1] - pos[1]\n  # Determine the direction to move.\n  if dx > 0:\n      dir = \"DOWN\"\n  elif dx < 0:\n      dir = \"UP\"\n  elif dy > 0:\n      dir = \"RIGHT\"\n  elif dy < 0:\n      dir = \"LEFT\"\n  else:\n      dir = \"UP\"  # should not happen, but safe to have a default\n  \n  # Now, we need to move the agent to the workshop.\n  # We'll use the move function to move in the specified direction.\n  # But note: the agent can only move to adjacent cells, so we need to move step by step.\n  # Instead of moving directly, we'll generate a sequence of MOVE actions.\n  # First, check if the agent is already at the workshop.\n  if pos == workshop_pos:\n      # If the agent is already at the workshop, we just need to use the USE action.\n      return [env.world.action_specs()[\"USE\"]]\n  else:\n      # Generate a sequence of MOVE actions to reach the workshop.\n      actions = []\n      # We'll move one step at a time until we reach the workshop.\n      # We'll use the same direction for all steps.\n      # The number of steps is the Manhattan distance.\n      steps = abs(dx) + abs(dy)\n      for _ in range(steps):\n          actions.append(env.world.action_specs()[dir])\n      # After moving to the workshop, use the USE action.\n      actions.append(env.world.action_specs()[\"USE\"])\n      return actions", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
