{"timestamp": "2025-09-13T10:36:09.178956", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # 1. Check if the item can be crafted (i.e., it has a recipe in the cookbook).\n  # 2. If not, return an empty list.\n  # 3. If yes, check if the agent has all the required primitives for the recipe.\n  # 4. If not, return an empty list.\n  # 5. If yes, then move to the workshop specified in the recipe for the item (using the `move` function).\n  # 6. Then, perform the `USE` action to craft the item.\n  # 7. Return the sequence of actions: [move_to_workshop, USE]\n  \n  # Note: You are allowed to use the following functions:\n  # - `move(env, dir)` to move the agent in a direction (dir).\n  # - `collect(env, primitive)` to collect a primitive item (which returns a list of actions).\n  # - `craft(env, item)` to craft an item (which returns a list of actions) - however, you are not allowed to use this recursively as it may lead to infinite loops.\n\n  # You may also want to use:\n  # - `env.world.cookbook.index.get(item)` to get the index of the item in the cookbook index.\n  # - `env.world.cookbook.recipes` to access the recipes dictionary.\n  # - `env.world.cookbook.recipes[recipe_index]` to get the recipe for the item.\n\n  # You are allowed to use the following classes and their methods:\n  # - `env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal)` to get the primitive requirements for crafting the item.\n  # - `env.world.cookbook.n_kinds` to get the total number of kinds.\n  # - `env.world.cookbook.kinds` to get the set of all kinds.\n\n  # You are allowed to use the following functions from the `env` module:\n  # - `get_workshop_index(workshop)` to get the index of the workshop (e.g., \"workshop0\", \"workshop1\", \"workshop2\").\n  # - `get_workshop_name(idx)` to get the workshop name from the index.\n\n  # You are allowed to use the following functions from the `craft` module:\n  # - `get_primitives_from_recipe(recipe)` to get the primitives required for a recipe.\n\n  # Note: The `env` is a `CraftLab` instance.\n\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
