{"timestamp": "2025-09-13T23:04:44.285205", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is already in the inventory\n  if env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[item]] > 0:\n    return []\n  \n  # Check if we can craft the item (i.e., recipe exists)\n  if item not in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n    raise ValueError(f\"Recipe for {item} not found in the cookbook.\")\n  \n  # Get the recipe requirements\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item]\n  workshop = recipe[\"_at\"]\n  ingredients = recipe.copy()\n  del ingredients[\"_at\"]\n  \n  # Check if we have all ingredients\n  for ingredient, count in ingredients.items():\n    if env.world.cookbook.index[ingredient] not in env._current_state.inventory:\n      return []\n    if env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[ingredient]] < count:\n      return []\n  \n  # Go to the workshop and craft\n  # This part is missing in the current implementation\n  # We need to add the necessary steps to move to the workshop and perform the USE action.\n  # For now, we return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
