{"timestamp": "2025-09-13T23:45:24.183900", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Step 1: Check if the item is craftable by looking up the recipe.\n  # Step 2: If the item is not craftable, return an empty list.\n  # Step 3: Get the workshop index where the item can be crafted.\n  # Step 4: Check if we have all the required items/primivitives.\n  # Step 5: If we don't have them, return an empty list.\n  # Step 6: If we do have them, go to the workshop location and perform the USE action.\n  # Step 7: The function should return the sequence of actions (move to workshop, use at workshop) to craft the item.\n\n  # Note: The function should only return a list of actions if the item is craftable and all required items are present.\n  # Note: The function must not return any action if the item is not craftable or if any required item is missing.\n\n  # Step 8: If the item is craftable and all required items are present, return a list of actions to go to the workshop and use it.\n  # Step 9: If the item is craftable and all required items are present, return a list of actions to go to the workshop and use it.\n  # Step 10: If the item is craftable and all required items are present, return a list of actions to go to the workshop and use it.\n\n  # Note: The function must not return any action if the item is not craftable or if any required item is missing.\n\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-09-13T23:45:26.627735", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is craftable. If not, return empty list.\n  if not env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item):\n      return []\n\n  # Get the required ingredients for the item.\n  ingredients = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item]\n  # Get the workshop location where the item can be crafted.\n  workshop = ingredients[\"_at\"]\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.index[workshop]\n\n  # Check if we have all the required ingredients.\n  inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  for ingr, count in ingredients.items():\n      if ingr == \"_at\":\n          continue\n      if inventory[ingr] < count:\n          # If any ingredient is missing, return empty list.\n          return []\n\n  # If we have all ingredients, go to the workshop and craft.\n  actions = []\n  # Find the workshop location on the grid.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(env.world.n_features):\n      if env._current_state.grid[i, i, workshop_index] > 0:\n          workshop_pos = (i, i)\n          break\n\n  # Move to the workshop.\n  if workshop_pos is not None:\n      # Calculate the direction to move towards the workshop.\n      dx = workshop_pos[0] - env._current_state.pos[0]\n      dy = workshop_pos[1] - env._current_state.pos[1]\n      if dx > 0:\n          actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n      elif dx < 0:\n          actions.append(1)  # UP\n      if dy > 0:\n          actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n      elif dy < 0:\n          actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n      # Now perform the USE action.\n      actions.append(4)  # USE\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
