{"timestamp": "2025-09-13T23:53:53.927605", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # This is a helper function to check if we have all the required ingredients for the recipe.\n  def has_primitives(goal):\n    # This function returns True if the current inventory has all the required primitives for the given goal.\n    # It is used to check if the agent has all the items needed to craft a certain item.\n    # We can use the method `env._current_state.inventory` to get the current inventory.\n    # The `env.world.cookbook` holds the recipe information.\n    # The `env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal)` returns a dict of primitive items and their required quantities.\n    # For example: for a goal of \"axe\" which requires \"wood\" and \"iron\", the output would be {wood: 1, iron: 1}.\n    # We need to check if the inventory has at least the required quantity for each primitive.\n    # Note: `env.world.cookbook.index` is a mapping from item names to integer indices.\n    # The `env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal)` returns a dictionary where the keys are primitive item names (strings), and the values are the required quantities.\n    # We need to convert the primitive item names to their integer indices using `env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]`.\n    # Then, we check if the inventory has at least the required quantity for each primitive.\n\n    # TODO: Implement the logic here.\n    # We should return True if the agent has all required primitives, otherwise False.\n\n    # Step 1: Get the recipe for the goal item (if it exists).\n    # Step 2: For each primitive in the recipe, check if the inventory has enough.\n    # Step 3: Return True if all are satisfied, else False.\n\n    # Example:\n    # recipe = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal)\n    # for primitive_name, required_count in recipe.items():\n    #   primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive_name]\n    #   if env._current_state.inventory[primitive_index] < required_count:\n    #     return False\n    # return True\n\n    # Implement the above steps here.\n    return False", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
