{"timestamp": "2025-09-14T00:20:02.635486", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Get the item index from the environment's cookbook.\n  item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  # Get the recipe for the item from the cookbook.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index]\n  # Get the workshop index where this item can be crafted.\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.index[recipe['_at']]\n  # Get the workshop location from the environment.\n  workshop_location = env.world.workshop_indices[workshop_index]\n  # Get the current position of the agent.\n  current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  # Get the current direction of the agent.\n  current_dir = env._current_state.dir\n  # Get the current inventory.\n  inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  # Get the required primitives for the item.\n  primitives = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item_index)\n  # Check if we have all the required primitives in our inventory.\n  has_all = True\n  for primitive_index, count in primitives.items():\n      if inventory[primitive_index] < count:\n          has_all = False\n          break\n  # If we don't have all the primitives, return empty list.\n  if not has_all:\n      return []\n  # If we have all the primitives, we need to go to the workshop.\n  # Find the workshop location.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  # Iterate over the grid to find the workshop.\n  for i in range(env.world.cookbook.n_kinds):\n      if i == workshop_location:\n          workshop_pos = np.argwhere(env._current_state.grid[:, :, i] == 1)\n          if len(workshop_pos) > 0:\n              workshop_pos = tuple(workshop_pos[0])\n              break\n  # If workshop is not found, return empty list.\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n      return []\n  # Calculate the direction to face the workshop.\n  dx = workshop_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n  dy = workshop_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n  # Determine the direction to move.\n  if dx == 0 and dy == 0:\n      # Already at the workshop, just use.\n      return [4]  # USE action\n  elif dx == 0:\n      if dy > 0:\n          direction = 1  # UP\n      else:\n          direction = 0  # DOWN\n  elif dy == 0:\n      if dx > 0:\n          direction = 3  # RIGHT\n      else:\n          direction = 2  # LEFT\n  else:\n      # If not aligned, move towards the workshop in a way that minimizes steps.\n      # For simplicity, move horizontally first.\n      if abs(dx) > abs(dy):\n          if dx > 0:\n              direction = 3  # RIGHT\n          else:\n              direction = 2  # LEFT\n      else:\n          if dy > 0:\n              direction = 1  # UP\n          else:\n              direction = 0  # DOWN\n  # Move in the determined direction.\n  # Note: This is a simplified approach; actual movement would require a sequence of moves.\n  return [direction, 4]  # Move in direction then use.", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
