{"timestamp": "2025-09-14T00:20:30.470065", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # This function should be able to handle multiple levels of crafting. \n  # For example, to craft an item that requires a complex recipe, \n  # you need to craft the intermediate items first.\n  # \n  # The function should check if the item has a recipe (if not, it's a primitive and we can collect it).\n  # If it does, it should first check if the agent has all the required primitives (or intermediate items) in the inventory.\n  # If not, it should collect the missing items.\n  # Then, it should go to the workshop specified in the recipe and craft the item.\n  # \n  # The function should return a list of actions to craft the item.\n  # \n  # You are allowed to use the following functions:\n  #   env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal)  # returns a dict of primitive requirements for the goal item\n  #   env.world.cookbook.index.get(item)       # returns the index of the item\n  #   env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive)  # returns the index of the primitive\n  #   env.world.cookbook.n_kinds              # total number of item kinds\n  #   env.world.cookbook.primitives           # set of primitive item indices\n  #   env.world.cookbook.recipes              # dictionary of recipes\n  #   env.world.cookbook.environment          # set of environment indices\n  #   env.world.cookbook.kinds                # set of all item indices\n  #   env.world.cookbook.index                # index object mapping item names to indices\n  #   env.world.cookbook.recipes[goal]        # recipe for the goal item\n  #   env.world.cookbook.recipes[goal]._at    # workshop location for the goal item\n  #   env.world.cookbook.recipes[goal].keys() # recipe ingredients (excluding _at)\n  #\n  # The function should return a list of action indices (0-4) to craft the item.\n\n  return []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
