{"timestamp": "2025-09-14T00:25:25.316952", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Implement the code for craft_v2 here.\n  # We provide the following helper functions:\n  # - env.world.cookbook: Cookbook instance holding recipes, primitives, and environment indices\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index: Index instance mapping names to integer IDs\n  # - env.world.cookbook.recipes: dict {output_index: {ingredient_index or \"_key\": count}}\n  # - env.world.cookbook.primitives: set of int indices for primitive resources\n  # - env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal) -> dict: dict mapping primitive-kind indices (int) to counts (int) required to craft one goal; empty if goal has no recipe\n  # - env.world.cookbook.n_kinds: int (total number of kinds)\n  # - env.world.cookbook.kinds: set of all int indices (environment \u222a primitives \u222a recipe outputs)\n  # - env.world.non_grabbable_indices: set of int indices for entities that cannot be picked up\n  # - env.world.grabbable_indices: list of int indices for entities that can be picked up\n  # - env.world.workshop_indices: list of int indices for different types workshop locations\n  # - env.world.water_index: int index for the \u201cwater\u201d entity\n  # - env.world.stone_index: int index for the \u201cstone\u201d entity\n\n  # We also provide the following functions from the CraftState:\n  # - env._current_state.features: 1D float32 array of length n_features\n  # - env._current_state.satisfies(goal_name, goal_arg) -> bool: True if inventory[goal_arg] > 0, else False\n  # - env._current_state.next_to(i_kind) -> bool: True if any cell in the 3\u00d73 neighborhood around pos contains that kind, else False\n  # - env._current_state.step(action) -> (float, CraftState)\n  # - env._current_state.step(action) -> (float, CraftState) returns reward and new state\n  # - env._current_state.features_dict: dict with keys \"features_ego\", \"features_ego_large\", \"features_global\", \"pos\", \"direction\", \"inventory\"\n  # - env._current_state.inventory: numpy.ndarray of length n_kinds\n\n  # Note: The `env` is a CraftLab instance, so you can use `env._current_state` to get the current state.\n\n  # We also provide the following helper functions:\n  # - `get_recipe_info(item)` (defined below) that returns:\n  #     - workshop_index: index of the workshop where the item can be crafted\n  #     - recipe: dict of {ingredient: count} for the recipe\n  #     - primitives_needed: dict of {primitive: count} for the recipe\n  #     - has_primitives: bool indicating if all primitives are present in inventory\n\n  # This is a helper function to get recipe info for an item.\n  def get_recipe_info(item):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns:\n      workshop_index: index of the workshop where the item can be crafted\n      recipe: dict of {ingredient: count} for the recipe\n      primitives_needed: dict of {primitive: count} for the recipe\n      has_primitives: bool indicating if all primitives are present in inventory\n    \"\"\"\n    # Get the item index from the cookbook index\n    item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n    # Get the recipe for the item index\n    recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item_index, {})\n    # Get the workshop index from the recipe (the key \"_key\" points to the workshop)\n    workshop_index = recipe.get(\"_key\", None)\n    if workshop_index is None:\n      # If no workshop is specified, return an error\n      raise ValueError(f\"Recipe for {item} does not specify a workshop.\")\n    \n    # Get the primitive requirements for the item\n    primitives_needed = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item_index)\n    # Check if we have all the primitives\n    has_primitives = True\n    for primitive, count in primitives_needed.items():\n      # Check if the primitive is in the inventory\n      if env._current_state.inventory[primitive] < count:\n        has_primitives = False\n        break\n    \n    return workshop_index, recipe, primitives_needed, has_primitives\n\n  # We will now implement the main logic for craft_v2.\n  # First, get the recipe info for the item.\n  workshop_index, recipe, primitives_needed, has_primitives = get_recipe_info(item)\n\n  # If we don't have all the primitives, we need to collect them.\n  if not has_primitives:\n    # We will collect each primitive needed.\n    # For each primitive needed, we will call collect_v0 (which is not defined here, but we assume it exists).\n    # However, since we are only to return a list of actions for craft_v2, we cannot call other functions.\n    # Instead, we will return an empty list to indicate that we need to collect the primitives first.\n    # But note: The problem says to return a list of actions to craft the item. If we don't have the primitives,\n    # we should not return a list of actions that would fail (like going to the workshop and using).\n    # So we return an empty list.\n    return []\n  \n  # Now, we need to go to the workshop and craft the item.\n  # First, find the workshop location.\n  # We need to find a workshop of the type `workshop_index` in the environment.\n  # We can search for the workshop by checking the grid for the workshop kind.\n  # We'll iterate over the grid to find the position of the workshop.\n  # Note: `env._current_state.grid` is the current grid (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  # We need to find the position (x, y) where grid[x, y, workshop_index] == 1.\n  # But note: workshop_index is the index of the workshop kind (e.g., 0 for WORKSHOP0, 1 for WORKSHOP1, etc.)\n  # However, the workshop kind index might not be the same as the workshop index we have (which is the index of the workshop kind).\n  # Actually, workshop_index is the index of the workshop kind (e.g., 0 for WORKSHOP0, 1 for WORKSHOP1, 2 for WORKSHOP2).\n  # So we are looking for a cell where the workshop kind (workshop_index) is present.\n\n  # Let's find the workshop location.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  # Get the current grid\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  # The grid has dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n  # We are going to search for a cell where grid[x, y, workshop_index] == 1\n  # We'll iterate over all positions in the grid.\n  for x in range(grid.shape[0]):\n    for y in range(grid.shape[1]):\n      if grid[x, y, workshop_index] == 1:\n        workshop_pos = (x, y)\n        break\n    if workshop_pos is not None:\n      break\n\n  # If we didn't find a workshop, then we cannot craft the item.\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n    # Return empty list because we can't find the workshop.\n    return []\n\n  # Now, we need to move to the workshop.\n  # We'll compute the path from the current position to the workshop.\n  # But note: the environment does not have a pathfinding function, so we'll use a simple path (by moving in the direction of the workshop).\n  # We'll move horizontally first, then vertically, or vice versa.\n  # However, the environment only supports moving one step at a time (LEFT, RIGHT, UP, DOWN).\n  # We can use the current position to compute the relative position to the workshop.\n\n  # Get the current position of the agent.\n  current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  # Compute the direction to move.\n  # We'll move towards the workshop by:\n  #   - Moving horizontally until the x-coordinate matches, then vertically.\n  #   - Alternatively, we can move in the direction that reduces the Manhattan distance.\n\n  # Let's compute the relative position.\n  dx = workshop_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n  dy = workshop_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n\n  # We'll move horizontally first (if dx != 0), then vertically (if dy != 0).\n  actions = []\n  # Move horizontally (x direction)\n  if dx > 0:\n    # Move right\n    actions.extend([3] * dx)  # 3 is RIGHT\n  elif dx < 0:\n    # Move left\n    actions.extend([2] * (-dx))  # 2 is LEFT\n\n  # Move vertically (y direction)\n  if dy > 0:\n    # Move down\n    actions.extend([1] * dy)  # 1 is DOWN\n  elif dy < 0:\n    # Move up\n    actions.extend([0] * (-dy))  # 0 is UP\n\n  # Now, we are at the workshop. We need to use the workshop to craft the item.\n  # The USE action is 4.\n  actions.append(4)\n\n  # Return the list of actions.\n  return actions", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
